From: shaohong.dong <shaohong.dong.cq@gmail.com>
Subject: [PATCH] i2c: qcom-cci: initialize completions for disabled masters

Controller reset always waits on master 0, even when only master 1 has
an available DT child. Initialize all hardware master completions before
requesting the interrupt or resetting the controller. This also covers
the unconditional master halt path during removal.

Upstream-Status: Pending
Signed-off-by: shaohong.dong <shaohong.dong.cq@gmail.com>
---
--- a/drivers/i2c/busses/i2c-qcom-cci.c
+++ b/drivers/i2c/busses/i2c-qcom-cci.c
@@ -536,6 +536,10 @@
 	if (!cci->data)
 		return -ENOENT;
 
+	/* Reset and IRQ handling use completions even for disabled masters. */
+	for (i = 0; i < cci->data->num_masters; i++)
+		init_completion(&cci->master[i].irq_complete);
+
 	for_each_available_child_of_node(dev->of_node, child) {
 		struct cci_master *master;
 		u32 idx;
@@ -572,7 +576,6 @@
 				master->mode = I2C_MODE_FAST_PLUS;
 		}
 
-		init_completion(&master->irq_complete);
 	}
 
 	/* Memory */
